ential so is every  American entitled to eat and his food  stamp something that ought to be that  ultimate guarantor I think that we we  know that given the necessity of  nutrition there could be a number of  ways that we could address that yeah  it's so you would you would vote to a  for a budget that cuts food stamps I  want to look at an entire budget look at  all of the details yeah is every  American entitled to eat well we've  determined nutrition is important yeah  you kind of can't survive without it  given the necessity of nutrition there  could be any number of ways that we  address that is every American entitled  to breathable air doctors have told us  air is important and I think on that we  can all agree right but given that the  air is so important do we want to make  sure that there's breed of breathable  air for everybody this is another clown  congressman no shock there but the big  thing is this is reflective of the  worldview of people in the Republican  Party no you're not entitled to eat  unless you earned it it's terrible for  our country as a whole to have people  going hungry well unless you've earned  having food you don't get food and we've  talked about this sort of strict father  morality as I call it and as others call  it as well with abortion right oh you're  against abortion hey great news we  figured out how to reduce the number of  abortions you prevent pregnancies and  the way to do that is access to birth  control and comprehensive sex education  nope you know why because on some level  morally if you have sex you deserve to  have a baby  well at least didn't use that right wing  talking point that making people  entitled to food would be tantamount to  enslaving farmers as right Rand Paul  uses when he's talking about health care  this is part of the affliction that  you're pointing out Pat of so-called  fiscal conservatism which is usually not  conservative in the long run and is  often completely immoral with hunger we  can fix this we could have fixed hunger  a long time ago if you look at food  production we've spoken to food experts  on the program before if you look at the  number of calories produced every day on  our planet and you look at the number of  people that live  our plan a pretty simple division  equation we have more than enough food  now to feed everyone but with food waste  as well as the lack of proper allocation  of resources we have people that are  hungry but it is a completely solvable  problem should anyone be surprised that  congressman Smith answered in this way  or that there are Republicans who just  don't believe everybody is entitled to  eat obviously not look at what just  happened in Montana we're going to talk  about that next  Montana elected a man to Congress the  day after he body-slammed a reporter for  asking a question so chances are that a  guy who simply doesn't think everybody  has a right to eat is also going to be  an elected official it's depressing to  watch but this is America today and you  know Republicans justify increased  military spending by saying well you  know all other freedoms come after our  security and everything else is  secondary or I think you can use the  same logic when it comes to food if you  don't have you're not entitled to food I  don't think you're entitled to much else  who's gonna be in the military if you  don't have food it's gonna be tough  obviously that's not the people in the  military have earned the right to eat  not everybody has apparently according  to congressman Smith you're absolutely  disgusting we really appreciate the  support of our sponsors including  today's sponsor tag add AB the hosting  specialist they've got a great special  offer for our viewers which I'll tell  you about in a second whether you are  looking for cloud server solutions  virtual private server dedicated server  solutions custom server solutions  colocation services whatever you're  looking for tag a DAB offers it and  they'r